// tank_hull.coscad -- Terra II's heavy unit, the hull: two tracks, a body,
// a sloped glacis, a rear deck and twin exhausts.  Z up, +Y forward, the
// hull centred in X and sitting on z = 0; 1 unit = 1 board unit (the
// turret file shares the frame, pivot at the origin, and sits on the
// hull's top at z = 0.75).
//
// Plain ▬ is a corner-origin cube([x,y,z]): every part is written as
// χ (cx - x/2) (ψ (cy - y/2) (ζ (cz - z/2) (▬ x y z))) for a centre (cx,cy,cz).

// tracks: 0.4 wide, the full 2.2 length, 0.44 tall, at x = +-0.55
track_l = χ -0.75 (ψ -1.1 (ζ 0 (▬ 0.4 2.2 0.44)))
track_r = χ 0.35 (ψ -1.1 (ζ 0 (▬ 0.4 2.2 0.44)))

// the body between the tracks, z 0.25..0.75
body = χ -0.65 (ψ -0.95 (ζ 0.25 (▬ 1.3 1.9 0.5)))

// the glacis: a 1.3 x 0.55 x 0.14 plate rotated 35 deg back about X,
// centred at (0, 0.95, 0.6) -- built centred at the origin, rotated, moved
glacis = ψ 0.95 (ζ 0.6 (θ -35 (χ -0.65 (ψ -0.275 (ζ -0.07 (▬ 1.3 0.55 0.14))))))

// engine deck at the rear, raised
deck = χ -0.45 (ψ -1.0 (ζ 0.75 (▬ 0.9 0.3 0.1)))

// twin exhausts
exhaust_l = χ -0.55 (ψ -1.0 (ζ 0.8 (▬ 0.12 0.12 0.16)))
exhaust_r = χ 0.43 (ψ -1.0 (ζ 0.8 (▬ 0.12 0.12 0.16)))

main = track_l ⊕ track_r ⊕ body ⊕ glacis ⊕ deck ⊕ exhaust_l ⊕ exhaust_r
